o  like schedule time to learn stuff I  don't set aside X amount of hours to  learn about this new framework or  anything I will maybe if I'm very  curious about that framework find a  project that will help me use that  project basically but yeah having a  purpose helps me stay motivated in  learning stuff and it means a lot of  failing and a lot of hard stuff along  the way to figure out what I need to do  and accepting the fact that I suck at a  lot of stuff but I mean that's how you  learn and that is ultimately I feel like  how you become a lifelong learner I mean  it really it's a little it's kind of a  lesson on humility I think and the best  part is that the Internet has opened up  so many new ways of learning and  consuming content because of all the  amazing content creators out there I  personally learned the best from video  content so I'm really happy to say that  Skillshare has kindly sponsored this  video today for those of you who don't  know Skillshare is an online learning  community with over 25,000 classes on  everything from design to web  development to business to lifestyle  stuff literally anything you want to  learn it's on Skillshare since I've been  doing I allotment for like my whole  entire career I've been really curious  about web development  I found this awesome course by  Christopher Dodd on Skillshare called  understanding web development a  beginner's guide to the web it talks  everything about the difference between  front-end and back-end as well as things  like CSS JavaScript HTML really the  foundational stuff that's really  important to get started in what  development I also really like this  other class that I took called  discovering success 7 exercises to incur  your purpose passion and path by Emma  Gannon so taking this class with really  interactive materials and in video form  is the best place for me to learn and I  hope it will help you all to I mean if  you think about the fact that you don't  have to go back to co